  },
  question: "`service S {}` parses (the body is repeat(service_body_entry), zero entries admitted) and normalize refuses it with namespace_graft_body_dissolved_refused. Is an empty service admissible, and at which door is that decided? The claim an_empty_service_parses_and_is_refused_at_normalize_by_the_namespace_graft_holds records the measured behaviour only and is not a ruling; it goes red against an intended admission and must be re-pinned by that ruling.",
